      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "On these two rows, the generated kernel runs one point four times as fast as the baseline. Shorten each row to one thousand nine features. Now the numerical check fails. Let's calculate a row we can check by hand. Three across, four up.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 16.755,
          "duration": 16.355,
          "until": 17.355
        },
        {
          "say": "Square three and four to get nine and sixteen. Their average is twelve point five. Add a small positive epsilon so even a row of zeros has a positive denominator. Take the reciprocal square root. Multiply both coordinates by that one scale. See how the point travels back along the same line? That is root mean square normalization. Now give the first feature weight one and the second weight two. Which way will the point move?",
          "start": 17.355,
          "end": 45.715,
          "duration": 28.36,
          "until": 47.915
        }
      ],
